<Base title="Affiliate disclosure" description="The straight answer on how cannedlatte.com makes money, and why it never changes the rankings.">
  <h1>How this site makes money</h1>
  <p>Straight answer: some of the buy links are affiliate links. If you click one and buy something, the retailer or brand pays me a small commission. You pay the same price either way.</p>
  <p>That commission has no say in what gets listed, what specs I publish, or how the rankings sort. The lists are generated from label data, and no brand can pay to move up. Brands can pay for a featured placement, and when they do it's labeled "featured" everywhere it appears.</p>
  <p>I run display ads too. Between the two, that's what pays for all the cans.</p>
  <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@cannedlatte.com">hello@cannedlatte.com</a>.</p>
</Base>
